meta {
  name: A date with no row is not in session
  type: http
  seq: 47
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-calendar/in-session?branch_id={{branchId}}&date=2026-11-05
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.in_session: eq false
}

docs {
  5 November is an ordinary Thursday nobody has said anything about, and the
  answer is false, not true. Absence of a calendar row means not in session -
  the calendar is a whitelist of teaching days, not a list of exceptions to an
  assumed working week. A school that forgets to populate the calendar cannot
  mark attendance at all, which is the safe direction for that mistake to
  fail in.
}
